    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{3}$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Q\\cdot {I}_{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{3}=Q=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/id": "04499536-ff77-57b5-a545-7dcfddbe6125",
